SCORE: SUCCFAN-CURV-RQ | behavior_evidence=4 | geometry_necessity=2 | novelty=2 | downstream_mechanism=3 | falsifiability=4 | implementability=2 | exploration_value=2
SCOPE: SUCCFAN-CURV-RQ | IN_SCOPE | Behaviour is computed from train-only transitions (E2) and the curved object is named with its location (per-prefix curvature through the Poincare conformal factor, at encode and decode, E12/E13); c_p -> lambda_p -> residual is one connected pathway and the three switches are declared. What is missing is specification, not scope: the explicit f_i -> c_p aggregation/normalisation is never written and the domain guard for 1 - c_p||x||^2 is absent, which is scored under implementability.
EVIDENCE: SUCCFAN-CURV-RQ | E1 E2 E3 E5 E6 E7 E10 E11 E12 E13
OBJECTION: SUCCFAN-CURV-RQ | The encode/decode pair multiplies the residual by lambda_p and divides the decoded code by lambda_p, which is algebraically the same as a per-prefix codebook scale: argmin_j ||lambda_p r - c_j|| = argmin_j ||r - c_j/lambda_p||. The "curvature" therefore acts as a single positive gain on a Euclidean quantizer, so the candidate is variable-rate RQ-VAE rather than curved quantization, and no per-node curvature survives as geometry.
COUNTEREXAMPLE: SUCCFAN-CURV-RQ | One dimension, prefix p, lambda_p=2, r=0.9, C={1.4, 1.15}: Euclidean assignment picks 1.15 (distances 0.50 vs 0.25) while the scaled assignment picks 1.4 (0.4 vs 0.65), and that scaled outcome is bit-identical to plain Euclidean nearest-code against C/lambda_p={0.70, 0.575} (0.20 vs 0.325 -> 0.70). Second, at c_p=10 the factor 2/(1-10||x||^2) is unbounded and changes sign at ||x||=1/sqrt(10)=0.316, so at ||x||=0.35 encode multiplies the residual by a negative number and decode divides by it; no clamp is specified.
RATIONALE: SUCCFAN-CURV-RQ | Behaviour evidence is a 4 and not a 5: E5 measures real fanout heterogeneity (top-1 successor mass 0.4375 in bin 1 against 0.0543 in bin 5, Spearman -0.973, 4895 items per bin) and E10 gives edge coverage, but the SID-side premise (hub prefixes actually collide their successors) is not measured in the bundle, and the per-item fanout coverage for the exact f_i used here is UNKNOWN; the bounded check is the per-item fanout histogram with counts per entropy bin over all training items. Geometry is a 2 because a matched Euclidean per-prefix codebook scale reproduces the assignment exactly, as the counterexample shows. Novelty is 2: it is a routine variation of the per-branch/global-curvature family, with only the "multiply instead of add a loss" formulation as a difference. Downstream is 3: the assignment change (level-2/3 code separation for hub prefixes) and the observable (entropy in the top fanout quartile, prefix-conditional next-code accuracy) are named with directions, but the chain has a gap that E6/E7 already expose: l1_br has gold prefix alive 1.000/1.000/1.000 at depths 1-3 and still the lowest recall, 0.04671, because T4 NLL is 9.03, so prefix coherence is not obviously the binding constraint. Falsifiability is 4: all three switches exist (c_p=1 with geometry on, c -> 0 limit, both on), a failure criterion is stated, and the per-quartile entropy diagnostic discriminates mechanism-idle from mechanism-active; it is not a 5 because "what would refute it" is only implied (flat recall with rising entropy is stated, the converse is not). Implementability is 2: the f_i -> c_p map is missing, the clip range (0.1,10.0) is chosen rather than derived, and the conformal factor's argument x is ambiguous and its domain is unguarded. Exploration is 2: it is a near-repeat in effect of a family whose members (successor_geodesic_coarse, successor_geodesic_coarse_v2, tangent_successor_residual) are all below the 0.062 Euclidean control in E6, so a negative would add little.
SCORE: cocond-markov-poincare-ot | behavior_evidence=4 | geometry_necessity=3 | novelty=3 | downstream_mechanism=4 | falsifiability=4 | implementability=2 | exploration_value=4
SCOPE: cocond-markov-poincare-ot | IN_SCOPE | The behaviour signal is a popularity-normalised directed transition matrix (E1/E2), the curved operations are explicit (Poincare ground cost, origin exp/log, Einstein/Klein barycenter, E12/E13), and the behaviour enters inside the Sinkhorn iteration of the same block that the curvature shapes, so removing either changes the plan and the codebook step. Numerical safeguards and cost are claimed; the quantities alpha and q are asserted to be measured but never defined, which is an implementability gap rather than a missing component of the coupling.
EVIDENCE: cocond-markov-poincare-ot | E1 E2 E3 E5 E6 E7 E9 E10 E11 E12 E13
OBJECTION: cocond-markov-poincare-ot | The diffusion operator is written (B_bt @ P) with P of shape B x K, so B_bt is a batch-local 1024 x 1024 matrix, not the item-level transition matrix; for an item whose training successors are not co-batched the row is zero and the diffusion is the identity, so the behaviour switch is inert for most items and, worse, the SID label of an item depends on which other items happened to share its batch, injecting batch-order noise into the assignment. The supporting cost arithmetic is also wrong by about three orders of magnitude.
COUNTEREXAMPLE: cocond-markov-poincare-ot | Take items i -> j with n_ij > 0 but i and j in different batches, which is the overwhelmingly common case at B=1024 out of 24556 items (probability of co-batching roughly 0.04). Then the i-th row of B_bt is all zeros, (B_bt P)_i = P_i exactly, and every subsequent Sinkhorn step is identical with USE_BEHAVIOUR on and off; the "diffused" plan is the plain curved plan. On cost: one (1024 x 1024) @ (1024 x 256) product is 2.68e8 MACs, so the stated three products per level over three levels are 2.4e9 MACs per step, not the claimed "5-8 MFLOPs".
RATIONALE: cocond-markov-poincare-ot | Behaviour evidence is 4: E5 measures the successor-entropy spread, E10 gives 118315 edges at mean out-degree 5.45, and E11 shows the current SIDs share a first prefix only 0.0907 of the time against a permuted null of 0.067, so "consecutive items land on unrelated codes" is a measured, auditable gap. Geometry is 3: Poincare distance as the Sinkhorn ground cost and the Einstein midpoint are genuine curved computations that a Euclidean squared-cost Sinkhorn does not reproduce, but the proposal never argues the curved cost against a matched Euclidean-cost OT control, and the residual handed to the next level is log_0(c_j), which returns the chain to a flat space and may absorb much of the curvature effect; it is not a 4 without that argument. Novelty is 3: moving the assignment plan is genuinely different from the ledger's rank, transport, shell, cone and residual-loss mechanisms, but plan diffusion is standard label propagation on a graph glued to a known OT quantizer, so it is a distinct computation rather than a traceable new one. Downstream is 4: the affected assignment (the argmax of a diffused plan and the barycentric code), the expected direction (higher prefix hit-rate, lower successor-conditional code entropy, recall above 0.065) and the two discriminating diagnostics are all named; the E6/E7 observation that perfect depths 1-3 prefix survival coexists with the lowest recall (l1_br, 0.04671, T4 NLL 9.03) is the reason it is not 5. Falsifiability is 4: behaviour-off, Euclidean-cost-off and both-on are all expressible as switches with a stated falsifier ("(a) rises while (c) does not -> decorative structure"), though the three are not shown to be matched beyond the cost kernel and B_bt. Implementability is 2: alpha and q are undefined, B_bt's scope is undefined, and the cost claim is off by three orders of magnitude; tau=median(D) is at least a measured, frozen scale and the eps/clamp guards are present. Exploration is 4: no prior round touched the assignment plan itself, so a negative would rule out assignment-level behavioural coupling for this programme, which is informative on its own.
SCORE: CURVCELL-SID | behavior_evidence=4 | geometry_necessity=2 | novelty=3 | downstream_mechanism=4 | falsifiability=3 | implementability=3 | exploration_value=3
SCOPE: CURVCELL-SID | IN_SCOPE | It names a train-only transition statistic aggregated into per-cell branching (E1/E2), an explicit curved operation (per-code curvature entering the rescaled Poincare distance and the commitment term, E12/E13), a single coupled pathway (behaviour sets s, s sets both the argmin and the commitment, the resulting partition re-estimates s), the three switches, and equations with a cost. The defect is numerical/dimensional rather than structural.
EVIDENCE: CURVCELL-SID | E1 E2 E3 E5 E6 E7 E10 E11 E12 E13
OBJECTION: CURVCELL-SID | The curvature enters only as a positive scalar divisor on a distance, d_B(eps,c)/s, so it is a per-code cell-size weight; the encoder can absorb it by moving the codes and the proposal admits this, and no matched Euclidean control (per-code weighted Euclidean distance) is argued, so the curvature's added value over a per-code Euclidean scale is unestablished. The declared geometry-off arm also collapses into the behaviour-off arm.
COUNTEREXAMPLE: CURVCELL-SID | Dimensional: s_new = log(1+B)/((d-1)R) with B dimensionless, d-1 dimensionless and R a norm (units of length) gives s in 1/length, but s divides the dimensionless Poincare distance d_B, so the product d_B/s has units of length; with R=1, d=32, B=8 the value is s=0.067 and every cell is inflated 15-fold, which moves the partition for a reason that has nothing to do with branching. Ablation: geometry-off is defined as "keeps the behaviour weights but removes curvature", i.e. s=1 for every code, which is exactly the behaviour-off arm (single unit curvature), so the two controls are the same run and the coupling cannot be separated.
RATIONALE: CURVCELL-SID | Behaviour is 4: the premise is the E5 stratification (bin means 2.7 to 41.4 distinct successors, top-1 mass 0.4375 down to 0.0543, 4895 items per bin) plus the E10 edge coverage, so heterogeneity of branching is measured; the cell-level statistic B[l][k] itself is proposed and its distribution on the baseline SIDs is UNKNOWN, and the bounded check that would resolve it is the histogram of B[l][k] and |A_k| computed once from the frozen baseline assignment. Geometry is 2: the operation is a scalar divisor on d_B, the natural matched Euclidean counterpart (per-code weighted Euclidean distance) would reproduce the same cell-size ordering, and the proposal's own risk list concedes the encoder may cancel the rescaling; the atanh nonlinearity is the only thing that might not be reproducible, and that is not argued. Novelty is 3: re-estimating the curvature field from the partition the quantizer currently produces, and using it in both the argmin and the commitment, is a computational difference from the static/global curvature and shell mechanisms, but it remains in the same curvature-from-branch-counts family, so not 4. Downstream is 4: the affected assignment is named (the level-l cell radius), the observables are named with directions (Spearman |A_k| vs B_k positive, H(next code | level-0) falling, recall above 0.065), and the null outcome is interpreted; it is not 5 because E6/E7 show a configuration whose depths-1-3 prefix survival is perfect and whose recall is the worst in the table (0.04671), which weakens the entropy -> recall step. Falsifiability is 3: a failure criterion and a discriminating diagnostic exist, but the geometry-off and behaviour-off switches coincide, so the three controls are not three matched controls. Implementability is 3: the pseudocode, refresh schedule, cumulative mean, clamp, detachment of s, and the +2-4% budget are all workable and differentiable, but the s formula is dimensionally wrong as written and the commit weight beta is inherited without the curvature scaling being dimensionally reconciled. Exploration is 3: it is a different failure mode (cell-size allocation via a fixed-point loop) from the rank/transport mechanisms, but it sits in a family whose measured members are all below the Euclidean control, so a negative is only moderately informative.